<Project>

  <!--
    Ships FrameLedger.Guard.dll beside the importing project's output.

    §S18 blocker 3, ratified 2026-08-04: **the Agent is the sole host of the
    guard.** This used to live in FrameLedger.Infrastructure.csproj as a plain
    `None` item, which MSBuild flows to every project that references
    Infrastructure — so FrameLedger.exe (the WPF UI) received it too, purely as a
    side effect of also wanting SQLite and detection.

    That is what made §S18 hard. `GetCurrentProcessId()` was rejected as an
    identity because more than one FrameLedger binary carried the guard, so the
    fix had to be a property of the DIRECTORY rather than of the process. Making
    the Agent the only host does not remove the need for the install-root check —
    the Agent is still the game's parent in launch mode, and still inside the
    §S16 scan set — but it shrinks the exposed surface instead of widening a
    carve-out, which §S18 itself called "the only candidate that shrinks the
    problem".

    Imported by exactly three projects, and each for a reason:
      - FrameLedger.Agent            — the host. It runs the guard.
      - FrameLedger.Infrastructure.Tests — GuardMirrorTests and
        RulesPathAgreementTests P/Invoke into the real DLL, so it has to be
        beside the test binary.
      - FrameLedger.CaptureHost      — added 2026-08-06. The unshipped driver of
        the guard loop (docs/HANDOFF.md item 1). NativeAntiCheatGuard loads the DLL
        by absolute path from AppContext.BaseDirectory and never falls back to a
        search, so it has to actually be there.

    THE THIRD IMPORT NEEDS §S18 BLOCKER 3 RE-READ, and this is that reading rather
    than a quiet exception.

    What blocker 3 was FOR was the WPF UI acquiring the guard as a SIDE EFFECT of
    wanting SQLite and detection — a `None` item in Infrastructure.csproj flowing to
    every referencing project. FrameLedger.CaptureHost is the opposite case: a
    deliberate host that exists to run the guard, in the same class as the test
    project that has imported this since it was written.

    And the fix blocker 3 produced is a property of the DIRECTORY, not of the
    process: `GetCurrentProcessId()` was rejected as an identity precisely because
    more than one binary carries the guard. A third one does not weaken it.

    WHAT IS NOT RE-DECIDED HERE: reversing a ratified decision is the owner's, not a
    PR's, and 20_OPEN_QUESTIONS §S24 records it as an open owner decision. What this
    comment does is stop the file asserting a count that stopped being true.

    NOT a cross-process hazard either, which a design panel proposed a named mutex
    for: §S28's fail-open is a race on PROCESS-LOCAL statics inside ParseRules and
    EvaluateImpl, and a second process gets its own image of the DLL with its own
    copies — which §S28 already concedes for the Vulkan layer in as many words.

    NOT imported by FrameLedger.App. FR-2.2's advisory pre-scan reaches the guard
    through the Agent over IPC when that exists (07_IPC); until then the App has
    no call site for it, so removing the DLL costs nothing today and prevents it
    quietly acquiring one.

    NativeAntiCheatGuard loads it BY ABSOLUTE PATH from AppContext.BaseDirectory
    and never falls back to a search, so it has to actually be there — which is
    the point: a guard that could be "not found" and shrugged off would be a
    guard with an off switch.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <FlNativeOutDir>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)build\native\x64-release\FrameLedger.Injector\</FlNativeOutDir>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="$(FlNativeOutDir)FrameLedger.Guard.dll" Condition="Exists('$(FlNativeOutDir)FrameLedger.Guard.dll')">
      <Link>FrameLedger.Guard.dll</Link>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Warn rather than fail: build.ps1 runs the native build first, so by the time
    this evaluates the DLL exists. A hard error here would make `dotnet build` on
    a fresh clone fail for a reason that has nothing to do with the managed code.
  -->
  <Target Name="FlWarnOnMissingGuard" AfterTargets="Build"
          Condition="!Exists('$(FlNativeOutDir)FrameLedger.Guard.dll')">
    <Warning Text="FrameLedger.Guard.dll was not found at $(FlNativeOutDir). Run build.ps1 native first; anything that calls the guard will fail to resolve it." />
  </Target>

</Project>
